[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Select the driver and point it at a dataset in %%PREFIX%%/etc/nova/nova.conf:

    [DEFAULT]
    compute_driver = bhyve.driver.BhyveDriver
    allow_resize_to_same_host = True

    [bhyve]
    zfs_dataset = zroot/nova

Host prerequisites:

  - /boot/loader.conf: vmm_load="YES" and nmdm_load="YES"
  - the dataset exists with volmode=dev and its images and instances
    children, and the nova user holds ZFS delegated administration on it:
        zfs create -o volmode=dev zroot/nova
        zfs create zroot/nova/images zroot/nova/instances
        zfs allow -u nova clone,compression,create,destroy,mount,promote,refreservation,rollback,send,snapshot,userprop,volblocksize,volmode,volsize zroot/nova
  - /etc/devfs.rules grants the nova group the zvol device nodes, one rule
    per container as devfs globs do not cross a slash:
        [nova_zvol=10]
        add path 'zvol/zroot/nova/images/*' mode 0660 group nova
        add path 'zvol/zroot/nova/instances/*' mode 0660 group nova
    and /etc/rc.conf selects it with devfs_system_ruleset="nova_zvol"
  - cold migration between hosts sends zvols over ssh.  Give the nova user
    a key and point [bhyve] migration_ssh_config at a file naming it:
        Host *
            User nova-migrate
            IdentityFile %%PREFIX%%/etc/nova/migrate_key
            UserKnownHostsFile %%PREFIX%%/etc/nova/known_hosts
    On every other compute host the nova-migrate user receives it:
        zfs allow -u nova-migrate create,destroy,receive zroot/nova
    and pins each sender's key in /var/db/nova-migrate/.ssh/authorized_keys:
        command="nova-bhyve-receive",restrict ssh-ed25519 AAAA... nova@compute1
EOM
}
]
